From 8e8edfa68e4f624bacc30c1bde476cb0565c0d19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:39:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/65] perf(chonk): release the final folding accumulator once
 the decider has proven it

After the tail kernel's group is batched, the decider proves the final
accumulator and nothing reads Chonk::prover_accumulator again (the hiding
kernel verifies the decider proof in-circuit, and ChonkProve works from the
hiding kernel instance and Goblin). Its two batched polynomials (about 4.8 MiB
on the headline flow) were still held through the hiding kernel's accumulation
and all of ChonkProve, where peak RSS is reached. They are now released right
after the decider proof.

Why the output is unchanged: only the lifetime of an object that is no longer
read changes. The decider proof is computed before the release, and no
transcript, randomness or polynomial value depends on when the memory is freed.
---
 barretenberg/cpp/src/barretenberg/chonk/chonk.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/barretenberg/cpp/src/barretenberg/chonk/chonk.cpp b/barretenberg/cpp/src/barretenberg/chonk/chonk.cpp
index f50ec08..f438c87 100644
--- a/barretenberg/cpp/src/barretenberg/chonk/chonk.cpp
+++ b/barretenberg/cpp/src/barretenberg/chonk/chonk.cpp
@@ -662,6 +662,9 @@ void Chonk::accumulate(ClientCircuit& circuit, const CircuitVerificationKey& vk)
 #ifndef NDEBUG
             verify_decider_natively();
 #endif
+            // The final accumulator is consumed by the decider; release its polynomials instead of holding them
+            // through the hiding kernel and ChonkProve.
+            prover_accumulator = ProverAccumulator{};
             goblin.prove_batch_merge();
         }
         break;
